        <p>CCCOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— The !Sanitary Works Committee are prepared to receive THNDIVIS for the sunply of about 45 tons per week of good Piring SLACK, to be delivered at Longford Depot. in such quantities as may be required from day to day, during the next six months. Perso. s tendering must submit, along with their tender, a 41b, sample of the Slack they tender for, and must name the Oit from which the Slack will he taken. The Contractors shall pay all persons engaged or employed by them the rate of wages, and shall observe the hours of labour and couditions of employment as defined by the Standing Orders of the Council, a copy of which may be Obtained upon application at the Town Clerk's Office. Tenders se3urely fastened must be addressed to the Chair- 'flan, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington, ftldorsed " Tender for Slack,'; and delivered not later than Monday, 2Pth September. 1904. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. Town Hall, Warrington, I. LYON WHITTI.B, 16th September, 19C4. Town Clerk.</p>
