        <p>"Dear Sirs,</p>
        <p>" I thought I would like to for- ward you the photograph of my son, taken after using your food nine months. He was born a fine child, but e -star led</p>
        <p>_lrcumstances let " him to be trought up on the bottle. "We tried several foods, but he "made no progress; in fact, we "had the doctor's opinion that at "three months old he was smaller</p>
        <p>"than at the time of birth. Every- " thing we gave him was repeated "back again, and he was gradually "wasting away. The doctor then "ordered ' Benger's Food' as a last "remedy. We immediately oh- "tamed it, with the result that we "could see he was making flesh "each week. You are at liberty to "make what use of this you please.</p>
        <p>"Yours obediently,</p>
