        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER. NORTHWICH PARLIAMENTARY DIVISION. REGISTRATION OF PARLIAMENTARY ELECTORS, COUNTY ELECTORS &amp; PAROCHIL BMW tORS, 1904. NOTICK Is HEREBY GIVEN, that DAVID ARCHER VAUGHAN COLT WILLIAMS, ESQUIRE, having been appointed one of the Barristers to REVISE THE LISTS OF ELECTORS. in Parliamentary Elections within the North Wales Circult,will make a Circuit and hold Courts for revising the Lists of Parliamentary Electors, County Electors and Parochial Electors, and also of the separate List of Persons entitled to be elected Members of the County Council of the County of Chester,though not en- titled to be on the Count Electors Roll of the said County, for the NORTHWICH DIVISION of the COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places following, that is to say : ON TUESDAY. the 27th DAY of SEPTEMBER mixt' , at 11-15 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day, at the Magistrates* Court House, Over, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts,v z. t—WINSFORD (OVER) POLLING DISTRICT —Over. WINSFORD (WHARTON) POLLING DISTRICT —Wharton. ON WEDNESDAY, the 28th DAY of SEPTEMBER NEXT. at 10-30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening of the same day, at the Magistrates' Court House, Runcorn, for the several Parishes and part of a Parish in the following Polling Districts viz. •—ASTON-B r-SUTTON POLLING DISTRICT—Aston Grange, Aston-by-Sutton- with-Middleton Grange, Dutton, and Sutton. HALTON POLLING DISTRICT—HaIton, Norton, and Stockham. RUNCORN NORTH POLLING DISTRICT—That part of Runcorn called Runcorn North. RUNCORN SMITH POLLING DISTRICT—That part of Runcorn called Runcorn South.—WESTON POLLING DISTRICT—CIifton and Weston. ON THURSDAY, the 29th DAY of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 11-45 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Town Hall, Middle- wich, for the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling District. viz..—MIDDLBWIOH POLLING D leY ; that part formerly known as CI le ro6xTtßonina—ndß°ltnei B vekrecrYoft ; Clive, Kinderton ; that part formerly known as Kinderton-cum-Hulme ; Middlewich and Stanthorne. ON FRIDAY, the 30th DAY of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 10-30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the liven- ing on the same day; on Saturday, the lit day of October next, at 10-30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and on Monday. the 3rd day of October next, at 10-30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Magistrate" Court House, Northwich. N B.—All the Lists for the Rural Parishes will be revised on Friday, the 30th day of September. and all overseers must attend at the Morning Sitting on that day. For the several parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz. : —BARNTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Ancierton, Barnton, Bartington, Cooshall. Cornberbach, Little Leigh and Mar- bury. DAVRNHAM POLLING DlbTßlCT—Daver.bam. Raton, Leftwich, Moulton. Whatcroft ; that part formerly known as the Parish of Whatcroft. MARSTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Budworth Great, Marston, and Wlncharn. NOR THWICH (CASTLE) POLLING DlSTRlCT—Hartford, Northwich ; that part formerly the Urban part of nartford and Parish of Castle Northwich, NORTHWICH (LEF T- WICH) P7LLING DlSTRlCT—Northwich ; that part fomerly the Urban Part of Leftwich and Parish of North- wich. NORTIMICH (WITTON) POLLING DISTRICT Northwich ; that part formerly the Parish of Witton-cum- Twambrooks. WEAVERHAM POLLING DISTRICT— Acton and Weaverlytm-cuir -Milton. WINNINGTON POLL- ING DISTRIC r—Nortbwich ; that part formerly the Urban part of Winnington ; Winnington t that part formerly the Rural part of Winnington ; Winuington : that part formerly known as Wallerscote. And for all and every the Parishes. Townships and Places (if any) within the said Northwicn Division of the County of Chester, for which Courts to revise the Parliamentary. Electors' Lists, County Elector" Lists, and Parochial Elec- tors' Lists therein, have not hereinbefore been appointed. All Overseers and other persons whose attendance may be necessary, are hereby require" to attend the said Courts at the several times and places aforesaid, at which the Lists of their respective Parishes are hereby appointed to be reviipe:', and all Overseers are required to produce in Court the Rate Books of their respective Parishes, containing the Poor Rates made and allowed during the period between the 6th day of January, 1903, and the 15th day of July, 1901, and to bring with them copies of their Lists and all Notices of Claims and Objections, and other papers they have received, concerning the Registration of Parliamentary Electors for the Northwich Division and County and Parochial Electors of the said County of Chester. REGINALD POTTS. Clerk of the Ches hire County Council. Chester. .30th July, 1904.</p>
