        <p>EDUCATION ACT, 1902. SECTION 8 (1) FORM 308 A, NOTICE. COUNT Y BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. LOCAL EDUCATION AUTHORITY. NOTICE I HEREBY GIVEN in accordance with the Provisions of section 8 (1) of the Education Act, 1902, that the Town Connell of the Borough of Warrington being the Local Education Authority for the purposes of Part 111. of that Act, prorose to provide a New Public Elementary School for about 1000 Children at or near the Avenue in the Orford Ward of the Borough of Warrington. The School will be available for the following area An area comprising the Bawsey, Orford. and Fairfield Wards. 3. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk and Clerk to the Local Education Authority. Dated 14th September, 1904. SECTION 8 (1) OF TEM EnucATlox ACT, 1902, PROVIDES AB FOLLOWS • " (1) Where the Local Education Authority or any other persons propose to provide a new public elementary school they shall give public nt,tice of their intention to do so, and the Managers of any existing school, or the Local Education Authority (where they are not them- selves the persons proposing to provide the:school), or any ten ratepayers in the area for which it is proposed to provide the school, may, within three months after the notice is given, appeal to the Board of Education on the ground that the propos Ad school is not required or that a school provided by the Leal Educatiou Authority, or not so provided, as ithe case may be, is better suited to meet tbe w'snts of the district than the school proposed to be provided, and any school built in contravention of the dvision of the Board of Education on such appeal shall be treate i as unnecessary."</p>
        <p>RDUCATION ACT, 1902, SECTION 8 (1) FORM 308 a NOTICE. COUNTY BOROUGH OF W ARRINGTON. LOCAL BDUCATION AUTHO 4ITY. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN in accordance with the Drovisions of Section 8 (1) of tile Education Act, 1902, that the Town Council of the Borough of Warn i ngton. being the Local Education Authority for the purposes of Part 111. of that Act,propose to provide a New Public Elementary School for about 500 children at or near Lower Wash Lane in the Latchford Ward of the Borough of Warrington. The school Will be available for the following area An area comprising the Latchford War I. J. LYON WHITTLE, Towia Clerk and Clerk to the Local Education Authority. Dated 14th September, 1904. SECTION 8 (1) OF THE EDUCATION ACT, 19C4, PROVIDES AS FOLLOWS : " (1) Where the Local Education Authority or any other persons propose to 'provide a new public elementary school they shall give public notice of their intention to do so, and the managers or any existing school, or the Local Education Authority (,here they are not them- selves the persons proposing to provide the school), or any ten ratepayers in the area for which it is proposed to provide the school, nay, within three months after the notice is given, appeal to the Board of Education on the ground that the proposed school is not required. or that a school provided by the Lois! Education Authority, or not so provided, as the case may be. is better suited to meet the wants of the district than the echo)i proposed to he provided, and any school built in contravention of the decision of the Board of Education on such appeal shall be treated as unnecessary."</p>
